{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_bdrk_0123J61AYEPJtKVMhXjnhH1W","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-4-7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now make all the changes in doing_prompt.go first.\n\nIn doing_prompt.go, I need to:\n1. Replace `WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_super_debugging_zh.md\", \"super-debugging-zh\")` → `WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_debug_skill.md\", \"debug_skill\")`\n2. Update the error message for failed write\n3. Add `WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_sense.md\", \"sense\")`\n4. Update `skillFiles` to include the new files\n5. Change `SetVariable(\"super_debugging_path\", superDebuggingFile)` → `SetVariable(\"debug_skill_path\", debugSkillFile)` and add `SetVariable(\"sense_skill_path\", senseFile)`\n\n\n6. Looking at the existing skill file writes around lines 122-135, I can see the pattern for how tdd-zh and testing-anti-patterns-zh are being written with their error handling.\n\n7. I need to continue that same pattern for the super-debugging-zh skill file, then collect all three into a skillFiles slice.\n\n8. The structure stays consistent: call WriteSkillFile for each skill, check for errors with the same return signature, then aggregate the file paths.\n\nWriting skill file handlers... Updating the variable assignments to use the correct skill file names and paths for the builder configuration. Updating variable assignments... Updating the variable assignments...","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd68a69a-0863-467b-9cda-9c279d856707","uuid":"1ea79c6d-23a7-4a31-abc1-88bc22591d16"}
